{"name":"Passion for Revenge","hex":"#dd0d06","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"passion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A true desire sustained or prolonged.","Any great, strong, powerful emotion, especially romantic love or extreme hate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To suffer pain or sorrow; to experience a passion; to be extremely agitated.","To give a passionate character to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passion"},{"term":"for","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Fore."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["Because."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for"},{"term":"revenge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any form of personal, retaliatory action against an individual, institution, or group for some alleged or perceived harm or injustice.","A win by a previous loser."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take revenge for (a particular harmful action) or on behalf of (its victim); to avenge.","To take one's revenge (on or upon someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Passion (2012 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Passion is a 2012 erotic thriller film written and directed by Brian De Palma, starring Rachel McAdams and Noomi Rapace. It is an English-language remake of Alain Corneau's 2010 thriller film Love Crime, but with the ending greatly altered. The film is an international co-production between France and Germany. The film was selected to compete for the Golden Lion at the 69th Venice International Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Passion_%282012_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passion_(2012_film)","wikidata":"Q3016883"},{"title":"Revenge","blocks":[{"text":"Revenge is an act against a person or group in response to a grievance, be it real or percei